PROTOTYPE ONLY (ADR 0027 proposal, new windows on the Linux host, docs/proto-new-windows-ubuntu.md).
Never include this patch in a build used for a trial, the gate or a verdict.
scripts/build-compositor.sh does not know it.

A patch against gst-wayland-display (https://github.com/games-on-whales/gst-wayland-display,
MIT License), commit 1301f86. Apply the four measured patches in scripts/patches first, in order:
render-on-commit, cursor-messages, windows, dialogs. Then apply these from scripts/patches/proto:
  gst-wayland-display-proto-second-output.patch (U0)
  gst-wayland-display-proto-second-output-on-commit.patch
  gst-wayland-display-proto-second-output-window-list.patch
  gst-wayland-display-proto-second-output-draw-before-copy.patch
  gst-wayland-display-proto-second-output-input.patch (this patch, step 3)
The lines of context are from that project and those patches.

The element with output=1 forwards upstream pointer motion, buttons, scrolling and keys to the
shared compositor. PointerMotionAbsoluteFor takes positions in the second output's own pixels
and clamps them to its bounds. KeyboardFocus gives the keyboard to the top window on the
requested output. CloseWindow asks only the second window to close. When keyboard focus is
lost, the fallback prefers a window on the first output. In the wayland.second-window message,
`key` is true while the second window or one of its popups has the keyboard.

Popups of the second window are placed relative to their parent, constrained to the second
output and drawn over the window. A popup under the pointer receives pointer input. Its grab
is allowed only while its window has the keyboard. A popup commit can release a waiting frame
on the second output when rendering on commit.

With no second output, the first output behaves as before except for two log changes. The
element no longer logs every upstream event at debug level or names an unknown key in warnings.
Outside this patch are dialogs whose parent is on the second output, resizing and more than two outputs.

